# The Dunce Rage Quit (2026-10-26, the owner's idea; third pass: "start fun, then get hostile super fast"). Now and then a
# bot asks something truly dumb in /faction. Three or four lines of fun, then the dunce snaps at the first joke, the
# realm smells blood, and it turns into a flame war: insults, threats, a cousin who is a GM, ALL CAPS, keyboard smashes,
# and a rage quit. "@exit A" logs that bot off for 2-6 hours once the scene has played to its end
# (AutonomousBotSchedule.RageQuit). A player who spoke during the scene gets a parting tell ("ragequit_tell"), and the dunce
# comes back sheepish ("ragequit_back"). Real swear words are not in the corpus (build_corpus.py BANNED): they swear the way
# 2003 chat did, wtf, stfu, gtfo, omfg, $#@!. Nobody uses slurs. The roasts call the dunce "they". New writing.

@kind debate
@realm *

